Torchlight: two tests in RenderQueue::processVisibleObject moved ahead of the work
they make pointless. Each render pass (the view, the light map, the shadow map)
visits every object of every node in its frustum, about a thousand in a crowd
fight, while the light map queues a dozen and the shadow map thirty:
- The visibility flags against the viewport's mask before _notifyCurrentCamera.
  OGRE 14 announced the camera to every object (LOD, bone-attached children, a
  billboard chain's vertex buffer) and only then rejected it in isVisible(). The
  mask does not depend on the camera.
- receiveShadows only when a shadow technique is in use. getReceivesShadows()
  visits each renderable's material; without a shadow technique the result only
  feeds receiverAabb, which only shadow camera setups read. The port has none.
What is drawn is unchanged. Not __SWITCH__-guarded: every target runs these passes.

diff --git a/OgreMain/src/OgreRenderQueue.cpp b/OgreMain/src/OgreRenderQueue.cpp
index 3de5fa283..b9e90d93b 100644
--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreRenderQueue.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreRenderQueue.cpp
@@ -254,12 +254,25 @@ namespace Ogre {
         bool onlyShadowCasters, 
         VisibleObjectsBoundsInfo* visibleBounds)
     {
-        // receiveShadows is a material property, so we can query it before LOD
-        bool receiveShadows = getQueueGroup(mo->getRenderQueueGroup())->getShadowsEnabled() && mo->getReceivesShadows();
+        // Torchlight: receiveShadows only when a shadow technique is in use. Without one,
+        // onlyShadowCasters is never set and only the shadow camera setups read what it adds to
+        // the bounds (receiverAabb); getReceivesShadows() visits every renderable's material, for
+        // every object in every pass. The group is still made here, as it was.
+        SceneManager* sm = Root::getSingleton()._getCurrentSceneManager();
+        RenderQueueGroup* group = getQueueGroup(mo->getRenderQueueGroup());
+        bool receiveShadows = (!sm || sm->isShadowTechniqueInUse()) && group->getShadowsEnabled() &&
+                              mo->getReceivesShadows();
 
         if(onlyShadowCasters && !mo->getCastShadows() && !receiveShadows)
             return;
 
+        // Torchlight: the viewport's visibility mask before the camera is announced. isVisible()
+        // tests it after, so a pass whose mask takes few objects (a render texture's) still ran
+        // every object's _notifyCurrentCamera - LOD, children on bones, a chain's vertex buffer
+        // - only to reject it. The mask does not depend on the camera.
+        if (sm && !(mo->getVisibilityFlags() & sm->_getCombinedVisibilityMask()))
+            return;
+
         mo->_notifyCurrentCamera(cam);
         if (!mo->isVisible())
             return;
